<task id="044" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Communication Actions PCF — Reply / Forward / Send / Save Draft / Save-to-SharePoint over existing endpoints (retires the 1,150-LOC ribbon send script)</title>
    <phase>Wave 4 — OOB form + PCFs (actions)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>8</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>020, 021, 022</dependencies>
    <blocks>043, 062</blocks>
    <tags>pcf, frontend, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>New PCF driving send/archive over existing BFF endpoints and hosting the W2 EmailComposer for compose/reply/forward; replaces a deployed ribbon web-resource (behavior-preserving migration); cross-cuts ADR-022 (PCF), ADR-028 (auth via host), ADR-012 (consume shared composer). FULL Step 9.5 gates required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-12, FR-13</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build a **Communication Actions PCF** on the OOB `sprk_communication` form that provides the communication actions — **Reply, Forward, Send, Save Draft**, and **Save to SharePoint** — and hosts the W2 `<EmailComposer/>` for compose/reply/forward. This is part of the W4 pivot to OOB form + PCFs (see `notes/W4-architecture-pivot-oob-form-pcf.md`) and **replaces the deployed ribbon web-resource `sprk_communication_send.js`** (~1,150 LOC × 2 copies) — folding in task 062's retirement.

    All server capability already exists — reuse it, do NOT re-implement:
    • **Send** → `POST /api/communications/send` (+ `/send-bulk`) via `authenticatedFetch` (ADR-028; host context supplies auth). Same endpoint the ribbon script calls today.
    • **Compose / Reply / Forward** → host the shared `<EmailComposer/>` / `SendEmailPage` (tasks 020/021) inside the PCF (or launch its dialog wrapper); wire mode + pre-fill from the record (reply → to/inReplyTo/`Re:`, forward → `Fwd:` + attachments).
    • **Save Draft** → `communicationApi` draft update (task 022) + Xrm save.
    • **Save to SharePoint** → archive the `.eml` + per-attachment Documents. The archival logic exists (`EmailArchiver`/`EmlGenerationService`; `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` per-attachment Document creation) but runs automatically on send/receive; expose it on-demand via a thin **`POST /api/communications/{id}/archive`** endpoint (NEW, small) that invokes the existing archiver, then the PCF button calls it.

    Retire `sprk_communication_send.js` (both copies) + its ribbon button definition once the PCF's Send is verified equivalent (behavior-preserving). Record the ribbon-audit result in task notes (this is task 062's retirement, done here).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke PCF + BFF engineer. Fluent in PCF lifecycle (ADR-022), `@spaarke/ui-components` `<EmailComposer/>` consumption, `communicationApi` (send/draft/SendCommunicationError), the existing send/archival endpoints, and ribbon web-resource retirement.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A PCF on the `sprk_communication` form exposing Reply/Forward/Send/Save-Draft/Save-to-SharePoint, hosting `<EmailComposer/>` for compose/reply/forward, calling the EXISTING `/api/communications/send` (+ a new thin `/{id}/archive`) via `authenticatedFetch`. The 1,150-LOC ribbon `sprk_communication_send.js` (both copies) + its button are retired with behavior preserved. PCF prod-builds clean; Step 9.5 gates pass; publish-size + CVE reported for the new `/archive` endpoint.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      W4 pivot (2026-07-15): enhance the OOB form with PCFs rather than replace it with a Code Page. Send + archival are fully built server-side (capability audit in the pivot note); the current UI trigger is the fragile 1,150-LOC ribbon script. This PCF consolidates the actions, retires the script, and reuses the W2 composer (which is otherwise used embedded in create-record wizards via SendEmailStep). Compose becomes PCF-hosted (or a launched dialog), not a Code Page.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (send endpoint; add /{id}/archive)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailArchiver.cs (existing archiver to expose on-demand)</file>
      <file>src/client/webresources/js/sprk_communication_send.js (RETIRE — ribbon send)</file>
      <file>infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/CommunicationRibbons/ (ribbon button def to retire)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/wrappers/SendEmailPage.tsx (host in PCF)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/communicationApi.ts (send/draft)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="pivot">Actions live in a PCF on the OOB form; reuse existing endpoints — do NOT re-implement send/archival client-side.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">PCF platform-library React/Fluent; lifecycle (init/updateView/destroy); auth from host context.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">All BFF calls via `authenticatedFetch` (host-supplied); no self-built credential; no `accessToken` props.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Host the shared `<EmailComposer/>`/`SendEmailPage` from `@spaarke/ui-components`; do NOT fork.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (§10)">The new `/{id}/archive` endpoint is a BFF addition: load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, state Placement Justification, report publish-size delta + CVE, add tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Retiring `sprk_communication_send.js` is behavior-preserving — verify the PCF Send is equivalent before deleting the script + ribbon button (this is task 062's retirement).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build PCF with `npm run build:prod`; deploy per pcf-deploy.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/notes/W4-architecture-pivot-oob-form-pcf.md</file>
