  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A PCF (`src/client/pcf/CommunicationActions/`) bound to the `sprk_communication` form exposes Reply/Forward/Send/Save-Draft/Save-to-SharePoint; prod-builds via `npm run build:prod`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Send calls the EXISTING `/api/communications/send` via `authenticatedFetch` (no re-implemented send, no self-built credential).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Compose/reply/forward host the shared `<SendEmailPage/>` (grep confirms no forked composer); reply/forward pre-fill from the record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`POST /api/communications/{id}/archive` exists over the existing `EmailArchiver` (on-demand .eml + per-attachment Documents), with tests + ProblemDetails errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`sprk_communication_send.js` (both copies) + its ribbon button are removed, with the PCF Send verified equivalent (task 062 closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; publish-size delta reported (≈ small for one endpoint); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    W4 pivot: OOB form + PCFs. Send + archival already exist server-side — this task is the client shell + one thin endpoint + retiring the ribbon script. The composer is reused, not rebuilt. Absorbs task 062 (ribbon `sprk_communication_send.js` retirement) — mark 062 accordingly.
  </notes>

